# .cursorrules

# Coding Standards & Architecture Rules

## 1. Paradigm
- Strictly follow Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) principles.
- Use ES6+ Classes, encapsulation, and inheritance where applicable.
- Separation of Concerns: Separate UI logic, Business Logic, and Data Access Logic.

## 2. PWA & Offline-First
- App MUST include a valid `manifest.json`.
- Implement robust Service Workers (`sw.js`) for caching static assets.
- Use IndexedDB for local caching of image metadata and offline queueing of actions.

## 3. Firebase & Backend
- EXCLUSIVELY use Firebase (Firestore, Cloud Storage, Auth). DO NOT use n8n, Docker, or external backends.
- **Firestore Pathing Strict Rule:** All document references MUST have an even number of path segments (e.g., `users/{userId}/images/{imageId}`). NEVER use odd segments for document references to prevent invalid argument errors.
- Implement strict Firebase Security Rules.

## 4. Version Control
- Commit changes logically using Git.

## 5. Refactoring
- When refactoring, RESPECT the existing OOP structure and offline functionality dictated in these `.cursorrules`. Do not break existing class contracts.